ype":"text","text":" lists every hyperedge once, a repeated one at each of its positions. A hyperedge’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position is its identity, as an edge’s is in "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions of the hyperedges a vertex is a member of, so a value keyed by "},{"code":"Hyperedges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a weight, is the same from every member. Positions are valid until the hypergraph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read incidence in index space. With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", so per-hyperedge state lives in arrays."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The algorithms in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" need both bounds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every conformer satisfies these laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"vertexCount == vertices.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"hyperedgeCount == hyperedges.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The members of a hyperedge are distinct vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A position ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a member of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedge at ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", once, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. ","type":"text"},{"code":"degree(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the length of that list and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"size(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the number of members, so the degrees sum to the sizes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(hyperedge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly when some hyperedge has those members, the empty set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included. It and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" never trap."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" is in index order, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members mapped through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"text":" in the same order, and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ofIndex:)"},{"text":" reads equal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the vertex reads.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With hyperedge indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedgeIndexBound == hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hyperedges"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"th position has index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Index-space members hash no vertex, and a vertex-space read looks its vertex up once."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Members with default implementations are still requirements. Generic code calls a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation’s own version when it has one, and a wrapper must forward every one. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol has no mutating members and does not refine "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Hypergraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","roleHeading":"Protocol"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a"},{"type":